    "updated_at": "2021-04-02T18:08:39Z",
    "body": "I was thinking about this and we can sort of do this now. If you set the following in your `starship.toml` \n```toml \n[python]\npython_binary = [\"./venv/bin/python\", \"python\", \"python3\", \"python2\"] \n```\nit should display the version of python from inside the venv. Note this will only work when the `venv` is inside the project and it will only work in the directory that contains the venv dir but maybe this is ok?",
