    "updated_at": "2021-04-02T19:37:05Z",
    "body": "> it should display the version of python from inside the venv. Note this will only work when the `venv` is inside the project and it will only work in the directory that contains the venv dir but maybe this is ok?\r\n\r\nAs far as I recall `pipenv` stores venv-s in `$HOME/.venvs` by default but there are at least two ways how that can be configured: https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/advanced/#custom-virtual-environment-location\r\n\r\nThere is also a [`--where` option](https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/cli/#cmdoption-pipenv-where) so something like this might work: `\"$(pipenv --where)/bin/python\"`? :thinking: \r\n ",
